whisper_cipher
==============

Write a function:

    def whisper_cipher(text: str, shift: int) -> str

Apply a CAESAR CIPHER to `text` with the given `shift`. Each letter is
moved `shift` positions forward in the alphabet, wrapping around at the
end. Letter case is preserved. Non-letter characters stay unchanged.

The shift can be negative or larger than 26.

Examples:
    whisper_cipher("abc", 1)              -> "bcd"
    whisper_cipher("xyz", 3)              -> "abc"
    whisper_cipher("Hello, World!", 13)   -> "Uryyb, Jbeyq!"
    whisper_cipher("ABC", -1)             -> "ZAB"
